WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.902
-My gosh, I am seriously so
excited to be here right now.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:06.072
Because everybody I went to high
school with is getting married

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.240 line:92%
and having kids, on Facebook.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
Probably in real life too.
But who cares, and --

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.412
And I'm not saying I don't want
to get married. I do.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.215
I just know I'm not ready yet.
Sometimes I think I'm ready.

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
I see the posts,
I feel the emptiness.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I want to be married.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.354
But then I eat bread and I feel
so much better.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.323 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:24.457 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh!

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:27.394 size:84% position:42%
Just needed some carbs,
almost ruined my life.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:28.928 line:92%
Like, that was a close one.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
You think you need
to get married,

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
just slam a sleeve
of Ritz crackers first.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
Make sure that's not
what you need.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:36.803
If that doesn't work, lie under
some warm laundry for an hour.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:40.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
It feels like being loved
unconditionally.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.341 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:46.780 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to have kids, too,
but I'm afraid.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:51.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because as far as I can tell,
you do not get to pick.

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just go to the hospital
in pain.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.989
Few hours later, they're like,
"This is what came out of you."

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You're like, "Really?"

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like,
"Yeah, no tradesies."

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.093 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're not cute
right away.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:04.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you seen a newborn
recently? It's disgusting.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's all --
it's all purple and wrinkly.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:09.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Congratulations,
It's a raisin. Look at that."

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:10.103 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we all have to lie
to new parents.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like,
"Oh, he's really handsome."

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"Oh, she's beautiful."

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:19.145
I'm bad at it. I'm like,
"Oh, that has potential!"

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
"What's --"

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.785
"What's that going to be, a girl
when the scales fall off?

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:29.456
Who -- who gave you a glue gun?
What did you make?"

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:30.156 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That needs like 40 more
minutes up in there.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
"At least.
What's her name, Salmonella?

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:37.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uhh! That is --
That yolk is running!"

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:42.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Not ready, not ready.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:43.036 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But I'm in my 20s.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:46.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
I shouldn't be making
any permanent decisions, okay?

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
Being in your 20s
is like having a virus.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.376 size:81% position:41%
You can't do anything,
you just have to wait

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.845 size:75% position:38% line:92%
until you're better.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.413 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:57.584 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:57.584 --> 00:02:00.520
And the whole time you're
waiting, everybody's like,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
"These are the best years
of your life.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are the best years
of your whole life."

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:08.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "I just used
a fast food napkin

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:09.796 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
as toilet paper."

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.131 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.700 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.136 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This gets worse?

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everything feels like that
in your 20s.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.038 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Temporary, pointless.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dating in your 20s is like
watching "Titanic"

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you're just like,
"This isn't gonna work out.

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:26.446
"But let's just enjoy this first
part where we're hooking up

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:29.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
in cars and pretending
he's not poor."

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:34.087 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.289 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Put a jacket on anybody.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:39.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hung out with some girls
my own age last week,

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:42.795
one of whom told me she's
writing a memoir at 23.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. "I'm like, maybe start
with a pamphlet."

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.969
Yeah, if you're writing a memoir
in your 20s,

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:53.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
you had better have been
murdered. Like --

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:53.773 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.241 size:84% position:42%
Unless you are murdered
or you're that chick

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
who got her arm bitten off
by the shark and kept surfing,

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.245 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
no memoir.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to earn
your autobiography.

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:05.018 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.086 size:84% position:42%
I will never hang out
with these girls again.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.322
At one point they started taking
photos for the Internet.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:10.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I don't know
if you know this,

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
but if you don't take enough
photos for the Internet,

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
you actually start to
disappear like Marty McFly

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
in "Back to the Future."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:18.965
Thank you for laughing, they did
not get that reference.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:19.632 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.902 size:81% position:41%
So this girl is taking
like 400, 500 photos

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:25.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
just trying
so hard to matter.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:29.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she turns to all of us
at the table and goes,

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:33.846 size:84% position:42%
"Okay, now let's do one
where we're laughing."

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:34.914 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:39.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then all the girls
around me went...

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:44.724 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:47.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
Feel how horrible that was?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
They didn't make any noise,
they just went through

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:52.865
the motions like an atheist
with their family on Christmas.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.734 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.734 --> 00:04:00.273 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a candid photo
to my generation.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.711 line:92%
Just a lie with a filter on it.

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you seen those
girls online?

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just like, "Oh, my God,
it's so weird

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:11.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
"that you caught me
in this poppy field

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:16.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
in my ball gown, #blessed."
[ Giggles ]

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.123 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.959 size:75% position:38%
No, that's not real.
And it's not candid.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:20.560 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Candid means bad.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.296
You guys remember the '90s
when you took a candid photo

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:24.497 size:84% position:42% line:92%
on a disposable camera,

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:27.834
and then you just didn't see it
for 30 days?

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:28.368 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:31.504
You went to bed every night,
like, "Hope that pans out."

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:32.438 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:33.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a month later
you picked it up

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.076
in that crappy paper taco sleeve
full of duplicates

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you need one for every
room of the trailer.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:43.616
And you went through and you
finally saw it and it sucked.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.418 size:78% position:39%
Three of your fingers
are in the corner.

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.720
Nobody's looking at the camera.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just your aunt and uncle
getting divorced

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the background.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.294
And you just wrote "pizza party"
in a scrapbook

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
like it deserved
to be a memory?

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was a candid photo.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.199 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:03.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys are great.
Thank you so much.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:06.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪♪♪
[ Cheering ]

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:09.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Come on, pal,
that's awesome!

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:09.909 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:12.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
Taylor Tomlinson.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:16.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
Follow her on Twitter
@taylortomlinson.

